            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cx7.json",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I would expect all of these to be in the base CX-7 file.  Any reason why they are not?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cx7.json",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Kevin Tung",
                        "email": "kevin.tung.openbmc@gmail.com",
                        "username": "kevintungquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Hi @patrick@stwcx.xyz, the reason all of these are not in the base CX7 file is that we introduced the MCTPI2CTarget configuration, which is not intended to apply universally across all platforms. Some platforms may want to enable this feature to dynamically set the EID and query sensors, while others may prefer to keep it disabled.\n\nThis separation allows each platform to decide whether to enable or exclude this functionality based on its specific requirements."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cx7.json",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This approach is creating the appearance of a new FRU though, which is not real.  We shouldn't be creating entity-manager configs for items that aren't real entities."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cx7.json",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't seem like a separate FRU, so we shouldn't create a separate inventory object for it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cx7.json",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not a Meta piece of hardware.  Why is it under the meta subdirectory?\n\nWhy is there no manufacturer?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "configurations/meta/yv5/yosemite5_cxl_board_vr_mps_tchip_stm.json",
                    "line": 306,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I suggest splitting this into two commits.  Adding the CXL connection can be done separately from modifying the nvidia CX-7 config."
                }
            ],
